"Graft signs in to claude.ai once for each account, in a window of its own, and keeps that sign-in in a web store of its own for that account. One sign-in serves Artifacts, Projects and Search Chats alike. It is used only by claude.ai's own pages and is never read by Graft or sent anywhere else. Signing out deletes it.\n\nSign in with an emailed code: enter the account's address on claude.ai's page, choose Continue with email, and type the code claude.ai sends. That is the one way of signing in Graft supports.\n\nGroups are kept by Graft on this Mac. Sharing with a group invites each person with the role the group gives them, and claude.ai emails each one, as it does when you invite them from the artifact's own Share panel. Where an artifact takes no commenters or editors, they are invited with the most it does take, never more." = "Graft signs in to claude.ai once for each account, in a window of its own, and keeps that sign-in in a web store of its own for that account. One sign-in serves Artifacts, Projects and Search Chats alike. It is used only by claude.ai's own pages and is never read by Graft or sent anywhere else. Signing out deletes it.\n\nSign in with an emailed code: enter the account's address on claude.ai's page, choose Continue with email, and type the code claude.ai sends. That is the one way of signing in Graft supports.\n\nGroups are kept by Graft on this Mac. Sharing with a group invites each person with the role the group gives them, and claude.ai emails each one, as it does when you invite them from the artifact's own Share panel. Where an artifact takes no commenters or editors, they are invited with the most it does take, never more.";

